Sure! To compare the declaration flags of your two objects, just pass their stringified forms to the `areDeclarationFlagsIdentical` function. If you haven’t already, you can stringify each object like this:

```ts
const leftString = JSON.stringify(parameterObject);
const rightString = JSON.stringify(variableDeclarationObject);
```

Then call the function:

```ts
const result = areDeclarationFlagsIdentical({
  left: leftString,
  right: rightString
});
```

The function will return a boolean indicating whether the flags match (with the special handling for optionality differences). If you’d like me to run the comparison for you, just paste the two objects (or their JSON strings) here and I’ll do it!
